issues.body:
In the timeseries panel, it currently is not supported to have duplicate timestamps. However, some users have information like this, and it would be useful to have this supported for visualizations.

One root cause to this would be if users have data with nanosecond precision, and Grafana only supports up to millisecond precision. This would cause some timestamps to be the same, even if the original timestamps were not. The feature to add higher resolution time options is https://github.com/grafana/grafana/issues/6252

## Feature demonstration steps

This is set up in [play](https://play.grafana.org/d/feavrpzb4wu0wa/kristina-demos?orgId=1&from=1970-01-21T05:40:39.458Z&to=1970-01-21T05:40:39.558Z&timezone=utc&var-fruit=apple&var-fuelType=Battery%20storage&viewPanel=panel-17), but the json is available below.

1. Create a timeseries panel with either 2 queries, or one query that is partitioned by a transformation - you will need two series for this.
2. Ensure results from the queries contain multiple data points per time.
3. Note that if only one series is shown, you see all data for a given time. If more than one is shown, you will only see the last point as provided in the data.


With the following, note that there are two series - both series contain two sets of values for two timestamps. When one query is hidden, you can see all data - for example, valueA at the first timestamp is both 3, and 6, with points shown for both values.

![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cad6087c-e611-4448-a004-1bf1ce40284e)

When both queries are shown, only 6 is shown for valueA at the first timestamp

![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/03be188c-808c-4221-a7a2-4abd1de2c990)

When duplicate timestamps is supported, we would see all points of data regardless of how many series were shown.

| Key | Value |
|--|--|
| Panel | timeseries @ 12.1.0-88106 |
| Grafana | Grafana Cloud (steady) // Enterprise |
