Related: https://github.com/grafana/grafana/issues/93069 Supporting time in XY may provide a good alternative to supporting this with timeseries.

**Why is this needed**:

Grafana does not currently support triggering a dashboard refresh from within a panel. This limitation becomes apparent in scenarios where interactive behavior across multiple panels is desired.

For example, consider a dashboard built using custom data source and panel plugins, where the panel uses Plotly for rendering charts. When a user zooms into one panel (x-axis contains numeric values), the selected numeric range should ideally be propagated to all other panels.

While Grafana enforces a strict separation between panel and data source plugins, a workaround using route query parameters can help share state between components. However, this alone is insufficient—without a mechanism to trigger a dashboard refresh, the data source plugin cannot react to the updated state.

In contrast, Grafana’s built-in time range behavior for time series plots automatically refreshes all panels when the time range is changed via dashboard controls or panel interactions. This ensures consistent behavior across panels without custom logic.

To enable similar synchronization for custom plugins, a way to programmatically trigger a dashboard refresh from a panel is essential.

**What would you like to be added**:

This feature should help trigger a dashboard refresh using the same mechanism as the [existing refresh behavior](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/blob/f65e501e1b9f325db6c484dde07989e44846ae2b/public/app/features/dashboard/components/DashNav/DashNavTimeControls.tsx#L41).

```ts
// public/app/types/events.ts
export class RefreshDashboardEvent extends BusEventBase {
 static type = "refresh-dashboard";
}
```

```ts
// public/app/features/dashboard/containers/DashboardPage.tsx
appEvents.subscribe(RefreshDashboardEvent, () =>
 getTimeSrv().refreshTimeModel(),
);
```

**Who is this feature for?**

This feature will be helpful for all users who are building custom data source and panel plugins.

**Why is this needed**:

The current pie chart label positioning doesn't prevent collisions or overflow, and on small charts labels can be rendered outside of the slice it it supposed to label making it hard to read.

**What would you like to be added**:

This still needs more research, but I think these would be good to look into as potential enhancements:
* Vertically center multi-line labels
* * offset first `tspan` by `-(lineCount - 1) / 2 * 1.2em` so text straddles the anchor. 
* Replace the angular calculation with a fit test, truncate overflow with ellipsis 
* Adaptive font size + truncation (similar to d3 and eCharts)
* Outside labels with leader lines + de-collision pass (similar to d3 and eCharts)
* Reserve space / clamp to bounds

Note: if anyone wants to tackle these issues please gate any changes behind a feature flag and break each line item above into a separate PR.

**Who is this feature for?**
Pie chart users

**Current behavior**
* The pie chart positions each label at the angular midpoint of its arc, projected onto a circle whose radius is the average of the arc's outer and inner radii ([getLabelPos](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/blob/b3c947ef066fcbedc6118a9e1ab1d997b79130c7/public/app/plugins/panel/piechart/PieChart.tsx#L443)), where the "inner" radius passed in is actually labelRadius — outerRadius / 6 for solid pies or innerRadius for donuts ([PieChart.tsx#L365](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/blob/b3c947ef066fcbedc6118a9e1ab1d997b79130c7/public/app/plugins/panel/piechart/PieChart.tsx#L365)). 
* Labels are rendered as an SVG <text> element centered on that [x, y] via `textAnchor="middle"` and `dy=".33em"`, with each label line (name/value/percent) stacked using `<tspan>` elements offset by `dy="1.2em"` ([PieChart.tsx#L377-L404](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/blob/b3c947ef066fcbedc6118a9e1ab1d997b79130c7/public/app/plugins/panel/piechart/PieChart.tsx#L377-L404)). Font size scales with outerRadius, clamped between 12 and 30/36px ([PieChart.tsx#L373-L375](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/blob/b3c947ef066fcbedc6118a9e1ab1d997b79130c7/public/app/plugins/panel/piechart/PieChart.tsx#L373-L375)). 
* Labels are omitted entirely for slices whose angular span is below 0.3 radians via the hasSpaceForLabel check ([PieChart.tsx#L367-L371](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/blob/b3c947ef066fcbedc6118a9e1ab1d997b79130c7/public/app/plugins/panel/piechart/PieChart.tsx#L367-L371)). Notably, there is no collision detection or overflow handling, so labels can overlap or extend beyond the SVG bounds.

